VulkanOptics (optics::)
======================

Reusable Vulkan material compositor. The host owns rasterization,
G-buffers, swapchain, photon-transport lifetime and command buffers.
No hardware ray-tracing extensions or cubemap/probe substitutes.

Reflective pixels resolve one BVH-derived reflection result, which replaces
the underlying rasterized surface rather than alpha-blending a second
reflection layer. The GPU stackless triangle BVH is shared with VulkanPMap.
Raster camera depth is decoded using VulkanGame's 0.1..1.0 viewport depth
range before tracing.

When a reflected BVH hit is also directly visible to the camera, its
actual lit screen pixel is sampled, preserving streamed textures.
Off-screen hits are evaluated from geometry, surface color, procedural
checker patterns, scene point lights and the cached photon map.
Matte off-screen reflections use a deterministic 3-ray cone filter.
Glass has pass-through, mattness, Fresnel and BVH transmission.

Individual photon deposits are NOT displayed. VulkanGame no longer creates
the caustic projector and does not dispatch it. Photon data remains
GPU resident only as an invisible cache for indirect lighting in reflected
surfaces. The optional caustics module remains available for future
physically normalized receiver-density gathering; it is not used by the
game's material renderer.

Limitations: off-screen mesh hits do not yet sample imported GLB textures
or skinned/animated mesh poses. Off-screen direct lighting approximates
the existing Point Cloud lighting and supports up to 16 point lights.
These limitations prevent pixel-perfect mirrors of fully textured,
animated scenes. Full-screen mirror coverage may exceed 60 FPS on M2.

Public API: optics/optics.hpp, optics/caustics.hpp.
Shaders: optics/shaders/compose.frag, raytrace.glsl.
